DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/hackathon-neurospora\n\nJoin 
 Chef-in-Residence Douglas McMaster and the Hill-Maini Lab at Stanford Univ
 ersity to give an edible MOLD a new name\, a new story and a new life on t
 he plate.\n\nTHE HACKATHON\n\nNeurospora is a bright orange\, fast-growing
  fungus that turns waste into food. It is also a mold\, which makes it a h
 ard sell. Student teams will rebrand it: a name\, a visual identity\, and 
 the stories and dishes that make people want a bite. Douglas works with te
 ams remotely first\, then on campus in March–April 2027.\n\nTHE PRIZE\n\
 nDouglas picks the winner. The winning design is used for a printed zine m
 ade with the design school community printshop\, posters\, and possible br
 anding for a food product.\n\nTHE TIMELINE\n\nNov 19th - Applications clos
 e\nDec 3rd - Communication Strategies Workshop with Jennifer Stonaker\nJan
  10th - Official Launch\nJan 30th - Winner chosen by the chef\n\nMORE INFO
 RMATION\n\nQuestions? Please contact Alessandra Massa at massaa@stanford.e
 du.
